<title>CHINA: Hong Kong April air cargo traffic with China.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong April air cargo traffic with China.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai was again the busiest air cargo route between China and Hong Kong, according to statistics for April newly published by the territory's Civil Aviation Department.</p>
<p>Shanghai-based China Eastern Airlines and Hong Kong's regional operator Hong Kong Dragon Airlines Ltd accounted for 2,192 tonnes in both directions during April. Beijing was the next busiest destination for air cargo with 1,542 tonnes both inbound and outbound.</p>
<p>Exports and imports, including transhipment cargo, in tonnes for April compared to March included:</p>
